#
#	aarch64-specific files
#
#	ainc-aarch64.$O is a real LDXRW/STXRW pair.  What it replaces
#	was ainc()/adec() defined in C in os/inferno/virtarm64 and
#	os/inferno/raspi3b, spl-masked and therefore correct only while
#	MAXMACH is 1 -- see doc/dis-numa-survey.ms and the head of the
#	file itself.  Everything else here is the portable,
#	correct-and-slow C, the same choice mkfile-riscv64 makes.
#
TARGFILES=\
	ainc-aarch64.$O\
	frexp-386.$O\
	memmove.$O\
	memset.$O\
	nan-386.$O\
	strchr.$O\
